"""Editorial questions for racing and disaster survival."""

from review_angle_plans import audit, revise_domain


RACING = """history_origins|How a Racing Series Began|Which rules, promoters, vehicles, and venues formed one competition?|Compare founding documents, early entries, and contemporary reports.
famous_examples|A Celebrated Race Reexamined|What made one race consequential beyond its finish order?|Use official timing, rules, strategy, incidents, and later changes.
hidden_stories|The Team Behind the Driver|Whose mechanic, marshal, medical, or logistics work shaped one result?|Use credits, crew records, and attributed accounts.
beginner_explainers|Reading a Race Result|How do classes, penalties, timing, and classification determine a result?|Use one event's official regulations and final classification.
advanced_concepts|Pace Versus Reliability|How did speed, tire or fuel use, and failure risk interact in one race?|Compare telemetry or official data with documented strategy and uncertainty.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|A Disputed Racing Incident|Which account of one incident fits the available footage and steward records?|Compare camera angles, telemetry, rules, and appeals without assigning unsupported blame.
technology_innovation|A Racing Design Under Test|Did one engineering change improve measured performance or safety?|Compare homologation, test conditions, results, cost, and rules.
people_personalities|A Driver's Decision in Context|What information did a named competitor have at one turning point?|Use radio, timing, team records, and contemporary interviews.
major_events|A Safety Change After an Incident|What investigation and rule change followed one racing incident?|Trace official report, implementation, and later evidence.
how_it_works|From Entry to Classification|How does one racing event handle qualification, competition, penalties, and results?|Follow a dated event's actual sporting regulations.
rise_fall|A Team's Changing Performance|Why did one racing team improve or decline?|Compare budget, design, personnel, reliability, rules, and competitors.
then_vs_now|A Circuit Across Eras|How did layout, barriers, vehicles, and spectators change at one venue?|Use dated plans, regulations, incident records, and attendance.
future_developments|A Proposed Racing Rule|What evidence would justify one planned safety or technical change?|Define outcome measures, testing, costs, and affected classes.
myths_vs_facts|A Racing Legend Checked|Does a popular fastest, first, or unfair-result claim match official records?|Check classification, timing method, rules, and date.
documentary_stories|One Race Through Its Records|How did a race unfold from preparation to final decision?|Build a dated timeline from timing, steward notices, broadcasts, and team accounts.
map_vs_ground|The Circuit Plan and the Surface|How did a track map differ from actual grip, elevation, runoff, or access?|Compare plans, inspection reports, and dated conditions.
route_choices|A Racing Line as Historical Evidence|Why did competitors choose different lines at one documented corner?|Use footage and publicly released data to explain outcome without coaching unsafe driving.
seasonality|Weather Changes a Race|How did temperature or rain alter one event's conditions and decisions?|Compare official weather, timing, tire rules, and incidents.
local_voice|Neighbors of a Venue|How do residents and workers describe a circuit's effects?|Use attributed accounts, noise and traffic data, and economic records.
landscape_process|A Track in Its Terrain|How did terrain and drainage shape one circuit's design or problems?|Compare engineering plans, field conditions, and later modifications.
accessibility|Who Can Attend or Compete?|Which cost, mobility, eligibility, or facility barriers affect defined groups?|Check current rules and venue provision, including alternatives.
infrastructure|Services Behind a Race|Which pits, medical facilities, communications, roads, and power systems are required?|Map public event records without operational vulnerability detail.
environmental_pressure|A Race's Local Footprint|What measurable noise, emissions, waste, or land effects came from one event?|Compare baseline, event data, and mitigation claims.
safety_decision|A Race Suspended or Stopped|Which published conditions led officials to delay, neutralize, or stop one race?|Read race-control record and rules; avoid implying personal safety advice.
place_history|Before the Circuit|What land uses and communities preceded one racing venue?|Use land, planning, and local history records.
comparison_of_places|Two Venues Under One Measure|Why do two circuits differ in safety, access, or spectator experience?|Compare equivalent specifications, event class, and dates.
responsible_access|Public Viewing and Safety|How did one venue balance spectator access with safety and local needs?|Use official plans, incident history, and affected voices.
field_training_method|A Driver Development Program|What did a documented training program measure and change?|Compare participant selection, simulation, track evaluation, and outcomes without instructional drills.
field_equipment_design|A Safety Device's Evidence|What tests and incident data support one racing safety device?|Compare homologation, fitting, real-world outcomes, and limits.
field_rules_and_fairness|Technical Rules and Competition|Who gained advantage after one equipment or scoring rule change?|Use official rules and comparable results, acknowledging other factors.
field_injury_prevention|A Measured Safety Improvement|Did one intervention reduce injuries in a defined racing series?|Compare exposure, reporting, severity, and implementation dates.
field_event_logistics|The Event Beyond the Track|How did transport, staffing, emergency services, and scheduling shape one race?|Use public plans, budgets, and after-event reports."""


DISASTER = """history_origins|How a Community's Risk Developed|Which land, building, or policy decisions shaped exposure before one disaster?|Trace dated plans, hazard maps, and social conditions without blaming survivors.
famous_examples|A Disaster Story Reassessed|What did one well-known event reveal about hazard, exposure, and response capacity?|Compare official timeline, local accounts, losses, and later investigation.
hidden_stories|People Who Kept Services Running|Whose care, transport, translation, or mutual aid work is omitted from the response narrative?|Use attributed accounts and service records with consent.
beginner_explainers|Hazard Is Not the Whole Disaster|How did exposure and vulnerability turn one hazard into human loss?|Use a bounded place and event with measured conditions.
advanced_concepts|Cascading Failures|How did failures in power, water, communications, or transport interact during one disaster?|Map dated dependencies and avoid a single-cause account.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|An Unclear Incident Timeline|Which sequence of failures remains disputed?|Compare sensor data, logs, witness vantage points, and investigation limits.
technology_innovation|A Warning System Tested|Did one alerting tool reach the people it was meant to reach?|Compare timing, coverage, language, accessibility, and observed action.
people_personalities|A Responder in a System|What could a named official or volunteer know and do at one decision point?|Use logs, authority, resources, and avoid hindsight blame.
major_events|The First Critical Hours|Which documented events changed the response trajectory?|Build a sourced hour-by-hour sequence with uncertainty.
how_it_works|From Warning to Relief|How did one community's alert, evacuation, shelter, and assistance systems operate?|Trace official plans versus actual delivery, without personal emergency instructions.
rise_fall|Recovery Over Time|Which services returned quickly and which remained disrupted?|Compare dated housing, health, infrastructure, and livelihood data.
then_vs_now|Before and After a Risk-Reduction Measure|Did one post-disaster change reduce exposure or loss later?|Compare similar hazards, populations, reporting, and residual risk.
future_developments|A Proposed Resilience Project|What evidence would show whether a planned mitigation project helps?|Set hazard, exposed groups, costs, maintenance, and measurable outcomes.
myths_vs_facts|A Survival Claim Checked|Does a viral claim about one disaster match official and local evidence?|Check timestamp, location, source, and corrective reporting without amplifying harmful rumors.
documentary_stories|One Disaster Through Its Records|How did an event unfold for authorities and affected residents?|Build a dated multi-source chronology with consent and privacy protection.
source_trail|Reading an After-Action Report|What did one review investigate and what was outside its remit?|Check mandate, evidence, interviews, findings, and implementation follow-up.
material_evidence|Damage as Evidence|What can a damaged building or landscape feature reveal about hazard intensity?|Compare inspection, design, maintenance, and alternative mechanisms.
chronology_dispute|When Was the Warning Received?|Why do agency logs and survivor accounts differ about alert timing?|Compare clocks, channels, language, access, and recall limits.
ordinary_lives|Daily Life After the Event|How did disruption affect schooling, care, work, and housing for one group?|Use consented accounts alongside dated service data.
power_and_institutions|Who Had Authority to Act?|Which agency or organization controlled a key response decision?|Read plans, law, coordination logs, and actual resources.
trade_and_exchange|Supply in a Disrupted Region|How did food, water, medicine, or fuel reach affected people?|Trace public logistics and distributional gaps without exposing vulnerabilities.
language_and_labels|Naming a Disaster|How do official categories differ from survivors' descriptions?|Attribute terms and explain effects on aid and public understanding.
maps_and_borders|The Hazard Map and the Losses|Did mapped risk reflect who was actually affected?|Compare map date, scale, exposure, vulnerability, and observed impacts.
conflicting_accounts|Two Accounts of the Response|Where do official and community accounts agree and diverge?|Check evidence, vantage point, institutional incentives, and missing records.
preservation_bias|Whose Experience Was Recorded?|Which affected groups are missing from the archive or survey?|Examine language, displacement, connectivity, and consent barriers.
turning_point_test|Did One Decision Change Outcomes?|What evidence links one response decision to measured harm or benefit?|Compare timing, counterfactual limits, and other conditions.
legacy_and_memory|A Community Remembers Disaster|How do memorials and anniversaries reflect different losses and priorities?|Use attributed voices and avoid flattening grief into a lesson.
field_strategic_choices|A Response Tradeoff|Which options were available to officials at one documented moment?|Compare public plans, resources, forecasts, and constraints without tactical prescriptions.
field_civilian_experience|One Survivor's Account in Context|What can a consented first-person account show about a response gap?|Protect privacy and compare with wider evidence, not representativeness claims.
field_logistics|Aid Delivery and Bottlenecks|Where did one relief supply chain fail or adapt?|Use public delivery data and after-action records without operational weak-point detail.
field_leadership_claims|Testing a Hero or Failure Narrative|Does a popular account of one leader match documented roles and decisions?|Compare authority, team work, evidence, and hindsight limits.
field_aftermath|Long Recovery|Who remained displaced or underserved after immediate response ended?|Use longitudinal housing, health, and livelihood evidence with affected voices."""


if __name__ == "__main__":
    revise_domain("045", "045_racing", RACING,
                  "Organized racing through event rules, timing, vehicles, teams, circuit conditions, safety evidence, access, and local effects.",
                  "official sporting and technical regulations, classifications and steward decisions, timing and released telemetry, incident investigations, homologation reports, venue plans, and community accounts",
                  "Name series, class, event, date, and rule version. Do not give unsafe driving instructions; distinguish official findings from speculation and compare safety outcomes with exposure.")
    revise_domain("046", "046_disaster_survival", DISASTER,
                  "Disaster events and recovery through hazard, exposure, vulnerability, warning, response, survivor experience, and long-term outcomes.",
                  "official alerts and hazard data, incident logs, after-action reports, infrastructure and service records, longitudinal recovery data, and consented survivor accounts",
                  "Use trauma-aware consent and protect privacy. Avoid victim blame, sensational survival advice, operational vulnerabilities, and claims of exact prediction; check current local emergency guidance before production.")
    rows = audit()
    print(f"Plans: {len(rows)}; reviewed question designs: {sum(r['status'] == 'editorial_question_reviewed' for r in rows)}")
